- live image proof is committed and CI-triggered; it could not run locally because this contained checkout has no `docker` executable/socket.

Deployment requirement: this changes the controller↔root-executor protocol. After merge, rebuild the executor image and restart/redeploy the container; an old running executor will intentionally return the stale-image diagnostic.

Remediation pushed on `775909c65`.

The initial Worklink patch was replaced/hardened rather than merely patched around:

- child fd 1/2 now target run-owned `0600` regular files directly; no pipe-buffer dependency remains;
- output roots are explicit and backend path components are validated; anonymous launch-error cleanup no longer dereferences `None`;
- the root executor protocol now carries per-stream caps and enforces them independently of the controller, reporting `output_overflow` in the terminal result;
- configured caps cannot be raised above the existing 64 MiB stdout / 16 MiB stderr maxima;
- enabled launch cancellation waits for the identity-bound handshake, then cancels and reaps the exact worker;
- direct children arm Linux parent-death SIGKILL with the post-`prctl` race check;
- the privileged executor integration test now uses the direct-output-fd API rather than the removed pipe API.

