The remediation now:
- makes authentication an exclusive ordered dispatcher fence: earlier handlers drain first, authenticate runs without waiter-slot consumption, and later work cannot dispatch until it completes;
- bounds graceful dispatcher drain and cancellation fallback, tracks/observes runner tasks, and preserves bounded cleanup under caller cancellation;
- closes the connection and drains queued handlers before marking the peer dead / retiring auth state;
- linearizes bounded queue publication against close and fixes concurrent publisher byte-accounting rollback;
- quarantines caller-cancelled owned requests and bounds abandoned-response tombstones;
- preserves teardown exception priority while keeping close-before-retirement ordering.

